    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fa4fa58d-0b37-465a-9bb9-d47546dee19b-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>(1)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><munder><mrow><mi>Na</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Al</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mo>&#34;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>&#34;</mo></mrow></munder></math></p><p>(2)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Al</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mo>&#34;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>&#34;</mo></mrow><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></munderover><munder><mrow><mi>Al</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>&#34;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>&#34;</mo></mrow></munder></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><msub><mi>xH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>So, when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> was leached with alkali to get <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> on passing of gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;forms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math> respectively are</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>Na</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Al</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><msub><mi>xH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p>",
